# The launch of a Structure gives no result (R22, item 3; plan M11 5b): the record of the launch in an operand position
# -- answer 5.
# Plan M11 5v: the declaration of the ordinary Structure lives in the data part of main, so the launch `S()` stands in
# the code of main, where S is seen; the root holds the call main().
sub: main () (
    S: (int: k 1)
)
    int: r S()
main()
